---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { GA_ID, ADSENSE_CLIENT, REPO } from "../consts";
const tracking = Boolean(GA_ID || ADSENSE_CLIENT);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What PhonePad collects: nothing. What this website collects, and how to refuse it."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated 11 September 2026.</p>

      <h2>The app and the companion collect nothing</h2>
      <p>
        This is worth stating first because it is the part that matters.
        PhonePad has <strong>no account system, no server, and no telemetry</strong>.
        There is nothing to sign up for, nothing to log in to, and no analytics
        in either the phone app or the Windows companion.
      </p>
      <p>
        The phone talks to your PC directly over your own network. It does not
        contact us, because there is no "us" for it to contact — no service
        exists behind PhonePad. You can verify this: the
        <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">entire source code is public</a>, and the
        companion never opens an outbound connection.
      </p>

      <h3>What is stored, and where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>On your phone</strong> — your layouts, your settings, and a
          key for each PC you have paired with. In the app's own storage.
          Uninstalling removes it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>On your PC</strong> — the same pairing key, the name your
          phone reports, and when it last connected, in a JSON file under
          <code>%APPDATA%\PhonePad</code>. You can delete it, and "Forget" in
          the companion removes an individual phone.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Neither is transmitted anywhere.</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      {
        tracking ? (
          <>
            <p>
              The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. It uses:
            </p>
            <ul>
              {GA_ID && (
                <li>
                  <strong>Google Analytics</strong>, with IP anonymisation, to
                  count visits and see which pages are useful.
                </li>
              )}
              {ADSENSE_CLIENT && (
                <li>
                  <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, to show advertising on the
                  documentation and guide pages.
                </li>
              )}
            </ul>
            <p>
              Neither loads until you accept the banner. Decline and no
              analytics or advertising script is fetched at all — the choice is
              remembered in your browser's local storage, which is the only
              thing this site stores without asking. Clear your site data to be
              asked again.
            </p>
            <p>
              Google acts as an independent controller for the data it collects
              through those services; see
              <a
                href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
                rel="noopener nofollow">how Google uses data from partner sites</a
              >.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p>
            The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. It currently runs
            <strong>no analytics and no advertising</strong>, and sets no cookies.
            GitHub's own server logs apply, as they do for anything hosted there.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <h2>GitHub</h2>
      <p>
        Downloads, issues and discussions happen on GitHub, under
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener nofollow">
          GitHub's privacy statement</a
        >. Anything you post there is public and is not ours to delete.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where the GDPR or a similar law applies to you, you have rights of
        access, correction, erasure and objection. In practice there is very
        little to exercise them against: the app holds no personal data of yours
        and this site holds nothing beyond what is described above. If you have
        accepted analytics and want that reversed, decline the banner or clear
        your site data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        PhonePad is not directed at children under 13 and collects no data from
        anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially the date above changes with it. The
        history is in
        <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">the repository</a>, so you can see exactly
        what changed and when.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue on <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">the repository</a>, or use
        the contact address in the repository profile.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
